we'll just run past them

40
00:05:39,710 --> 00:05:43,650
i think we could do it easy they don't move that fast

41
00:05:43,650 --> 00:05:44,990
that's true

42
00:05:44,990 --> 00:05:47,870
what do you think sound good

43
00:05:47,870 --> 00:05:48,830
sure

44
00:05:48,830 --> 00:05:51,350
any one of them could move

45
00:05:51,350 --> 00:05:54,350
so stay alert here we go

46
00:05:54,350 --> 00:06:17,810
get going

47
00:06:17,810 --> 00:06:24,810
they blocked us we can't get out of the way

48
00:06:24,810 --> 00:06:46,990
They blocked us!

49
00:06:46,990 --> 00:06:48,710
We can't get to the other door!

50
00:06:49,550 --> 00:06:50,790
What do we do now?

51
00:06:51,210 --> 00:06:53,490
There's only one thing we can do now!

52
00:06:53,490 --> 00:06:55,870
Go back the other way as fast as we can!

53
00:06:56,530 --> 00:06:57,830
Run for it!

54
00:07:07,270 --> 00:07:08,950
They're unusually aggressive.

55
00:07:09,770 --> 00:07:12,050
I wonder if we did something to tick them off.

56
00:07:12,170 --> 00:07:12,810
That's silly.

57
00:07:13,610 --> 00:07:14,870
They don't have any feelings.

58
00:07:15,010 --> 00:07:16,290
They're empty suits of armor.

59
00:07:16,930 --> 00:07:20,670
The only way to stop them is to find whoever it is that's controlling them.

60
00:07:20,670 --> 00:07:24,530
If someone was controlling those things, I didn't see them.

61
00:07:25,850 --> 00:07:30,170
Usually what happens is you get too close to them and then they attack.

62
00:07:31,130 --> 00:07:33,990
But these ones, they move to block the door.

63
00:07:35,190 --> 00:07:40,050
That means there could be something on the other side of that door they have to protect.

64
00:07:40,050 --> 00:07:43,650
Like whoever or whatever is controlling them.

65
00:07:44,270 --> 00:07:45,430
That's gotta be it.

66
00:07:45,590 --> 00:07:46,850
It's the only explanation.

67
00:07:47,490 --> 00:07:49,730
Then you think it might be a monster?

68
00:07:49,990 --> 00:07:50,830
I don't know.

69
00:07:51,130 --> 00:07:51,410
Maybe.

70
00:07:51,910 --> 00:07:54,690
Normal folks wouldn't have access to magic that powerful.

71
00:07:55,510 --> 00:07:56,550
What now?

72
00:07:56,730 --> 00:07:59,610
Unless we can get past them and through that door, we're stuck.

73
00:08:00,010 --> 00:08:03,490
We'll have to find the major whatever that's controlling the armor.

74
00:08:03,890 --> 00:08:06,410
Once we take them out, that should break the spell.

75
00:08:07,010 --> 00:08:07,570
Obviously.

76
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:08,790
I got it.

77
00:08:09,430 --> 00:08:14,470
If three people distract the armor, one of us can sneak right on by and get through the door.

78
00:08:17,690 --> 00:08:19,330
Good luck sneaking by.

79
00:08:20,930 --> 00:08:24,610
Actually, I thought you'd do the sneaking since that's kind of your thing.

80
00:08:24,910 --> 00:08:27,090
But fighting definitely isn't my thing.

81
00:08:27,750 --> 00:08:30,510
Living armor doesn't have eyes or ears because it doesn't need them.

82
00:08:30,990 --> 00:08:33,150
Stealth skills don't work on things that aren't alive.

83
00:08:33,930 --> 00:08:35,930
They don't have eyes or ears.

84
00:08:37,570 --> 00:08:42,750
Are you ready?

85
00:08:44,530 --> 00:08:45,750
Let's do this!

86
00:08:45,750 --> 00:08:46,050
Yeah!

87
00:08:46,750 --> 00:08:48,490
Come on, you rusty buckets!

88
00:08:48,630 --> 00:08:49,670
I'm right here!

89
00:08:49,810 --> 00:08:50,750
Come and get me!

90
00:08:51,490 --> 00:08:51,970
Ah!

91
00:08:52,130 --> 00:08:53,070
Bad idea!

92
00:08:53,430 --> 00:08:54,470
Don't fear, missy!

93
00:08:54,470 --> 00:08:54,730
Ask them!

94
00:08:58,630 --> 00:08:59,150
Oh!

95
00:09:06,110 --> 00:09:06,730
As they're mad!

96
00:09:15,730 --> 00:09:16,250
Ah!

97
00:09:16,250 --> 00:09:34,470
Oh, fantastic. There's one in here, too.

98
00:09:39,270 --> 00:09:41,870
This one looks different from the armor in the other room.

99
00:09:42,610 --> 00:09:45,870
There doesn't seem to be anyone here doing the controlling.

100
00:09:46,250 --> 00:09:48,870
I get the feeling this one's the strongest.

101
00:09:51,710 --> 00:09:53,570
I can't call the others for help.

102
00:09:54,410 --> 00:09:58,050
I'll have to fight this thing on my own and figure out what the armors are protecting.

103
00:10:04,530 --> 00:10:08,370
I'll try chopping off an arm or a leg. Maybe that'll slow it down.

104
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:17,390
Oh, God tiny ass.

105
00:10:17,390 --> 00:10:17,630
Oh, God.

106
00:10:18,250 --> 00:10:19,210
Oh, God!

107
00:10:19,550 --> 00:10:21,630
Oh, God!

108
00:10:21,630 --> 00:10:22,950
Oh, God!

109
00:10:30,870 --> 00:10:31,630
Damn it!

110
00:10:35,770 --> 00:10:36,450
Oh...

111
00:10:36,450 --> 00:10:36,470
Oh!

112
00:10:36,470 --> 00:10:43,770
It was protecting its shield.

113
00:10:44,770 --> 00:10:46,770
What the...

114
00:10:46,770 --> 00:10:50,390
What's that stuck to it?

115
00:10:51,450 --> 00:10:54,450
Wait, I've seen something like that before.

116
00:11:01,290 --> 00:11:02,510
That's right.

117
00:11:06,470 --> 00:11:08,390
It's a...

118
00:11:08,390 --> 00:11:14,990
An egg case.

119
00:11:15,750 --> 00:11:17,130
That's what it was protecting.

120
00:11:18,090 --> 00:11:18,510
Eggs!

121
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:23,730
What kind of eggs are they?

122
00:11:24,190 --> 00:11:26,310
Do they belong to whatever's controlling the armor?

123
00:11:26,930 --> 00:11:29,810
Living armor doesn't have eyes or ears because it doesn't need them.

124
00:11:29,810 --> 00:11:30,930
I knew it.

125
00:11:31,430 --> 00:11:32,730
There's more to these things.

126
00:11:33,450 --> 00:11:35,810
If it has no eyes or ears...

127
00:11:36,470 --> 00:11:38,750
Why'd it bother picking up the helmet and straightening it?

128
00:11:39,470 --> 00:11:41,510
Why'd it turn its head to track our movements?

129
00:11:43,050 --> 00:11:44,530
Why's it got eggs?

130
00:11:45,790 --> 00:11:47,010
I know why.

131
00:11:47,390 --> 00:11:48,670
There's a creature in it!

132
00:11:49,610 --> 00:11:52,170
There's no outside force controlling them.

133
00:11:52,690 --> 00:11:56,270
They move instinctively and deliberately to protect its eggs.

134
00:11:57,150 --> 00:11:58,210
They're alive!

135
00:11:58,210 --> 00:12:00,670
That means they can be killed.

136
00:12:01,810 --> 00:12:03,250
That means...

137
00:12:03,250 --> 00:12:05,450
We can eat them.

138
00:12:08,830 --> 00:12:09,830
Take this!

139
00:12:12,630 --> 00:12:14,030
There's too many of them!

140
00:12:14,910 --> 00:12:15,790
Oh, no!

141
00:12:18,790 --> 00:12:19,730
Keep moving!

142
00:12:19,950 --> 00:12:21,110
If you stop, you're dead!

143
00:12:21,210 --> 00:12:22,130
Behind you!

144
00:12:22,130 --> 00:12:23,970
Aslam!

145
00:12:25,830 --> 00:12:26,510
Wait!

146
00:12:26,790 --> 00:12:27,110
Wait!

147
00:12:27,210 --> 00:12:27,590
No!

148
00:12:30,590 --> 00:12:34,250
They can share their parts?

149
00:12:34,390 --> 00:12:35,170
Not fair!

150
00:12:35,310 --> 00:12:36,330
How's that possible?

151
00:12:38,330 --> 00:12:39,850
Hurry up, Lyos!

152
00:12:39,970 --> 00:12:42,910
We're getting swarmed in here and things are moving fast!

153
00:12:42,910 --> 00:12:46,250
It doesn't stop if you chop off its head.

154
00:12:46,830 --> 00:12:49,350
But if it's a living thing, it can be killed.

155
00:12:49,970 --> 00:12:51,830
My options are slashing at its organs,

156
00:12:52,270 --> 00:12:53,150
make it bleed to death,

157
00:12:53,770 --> 00:12:55,010
suffocate it, starve it.

158
00:12:55,610 --> 00:12:56,430
What am I saying?

159
00:12:56,490 --> 00:12:57,450
Those will take too long.

160
00:12:58,590 --> 00:12:59,570
First things first,

161
00:12:59,650 --> 00:13:01,810
I need to find out what kind of creature's inside.

162
00:13:04,050 --> 00:13:05,210
Maybe it's a slime.

163
00:13:05,730 --> 00:13:07,010
But they don't move with precision.

164
00:13:07,210 --> 00:13:08,050
They just...

165
00:13:08,050 --> 00:13:08,430
ooze.

166
00:13:08,430 --> 00:13:12,570
Maybe it's a horde of insects.

167
00:13:13,310 --> 00:13:15,870
No, I would have heard them scuttling around inside.

168
00:13:16,310 --> 00:13:18,150
Maybe there's a big spider in the helmet

169
00:13:18,150 --> 00:13:20,010
using its legs to move the armor.

170
00:13:20,870 --> 00:13:22,430
I wonder if that last one's it.

171
00:13:23,850 --> 00:13:25,990
I'm not gonna find out standing here.

172
00:13:26,890 --> 00:13:28,390
I can't overpower it,

173
00:13:28,710 --> 00:13:30,590
so I'll outsmart it.

174
00:13:31,430 --> 00:13:32,530
Yeah, this'll do.

175
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:35,230
I'll draw its attention and get right up next to it.

176
00:13:38,430 --> 00:13:47,990
I've got it.

177
00:13:49,770 --> 00:13:50,950
Now, let's see.

178
00:13:52,410 --> 00:13:53,230
It's empty.

179
00:13:56,190 --> 00:13:57,750
If there's nothing here,

180
00:13:58,310 --> 00:14:00,870
why'd that other one even bother picking its helmet up?

181
00:14:02,470 --> 00:14:03,330
He's coming.

182
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:04,390
Uh-oh.

183
00:14:04,850 --> 00:14:05,670
What do I do?

184
00:14:05,670 --> 00:14:10,090
Uh-oh.

185
00:14:11,570 --> 00:14:12,050
Wait.

186
00:14:12,470 --> 00:14:14,450
How can it not see me hiding over here?

187
00:14:15,330 --> 00:14:17,230
There's something about the helmet, then.

188
00:14:18,610 --> 00:14:19,450
What's this?

189
00:14:19,450 --> 00:14:30,950
What the heck?

190
00:14:31,290 --> 00:14:32,350
It's a mollusk.

191
00:14:32,810 --> 00:14:34,550
And right between the layers of plating.

192
00:14:35,230 --> 00:14:37,710
That's why cutting parts off the armor didn't work.

193
00:14:38,230 --> 00:14:39,830
There's a colony of these in it.

194
00:14:40,650 --> 00:14:42,270
It's still looking for its head.

195
00:14:43,570 --> 00:14:44,410
All right, then.

196
00:14:45,010 --> 00:14:45,450
Here!

197
00:14:45,450 --> 00:14:45,510
Here!

198
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:45,570
Here!

199
00:14:45,570 --> 00:14:45,590
Here!

200
00:14:49,450 --> 00:15:03,870
Now we're talking.

201
00:15:04,470 --> 00:15:05,750
This must be filled with them.

202
00:15:07,570 --> 00:15:09,830
Looks like they connect to each other at the joints,

203
00:15:10,050 --> 00:15:12,570
then expand and contract like muscles to move around.

204
00:15:13,290 --> 00:15:14,870
But which one laid the eggs?

205
00:15:15,330 --> 00:15:16,750
Guess if they're hermaphrodites,

206
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:17,770
guess they all could have laid them.

207
00:15:19,510 --> 00:15:21,330
Now's not the time to think about that.

208
00:15:23,030 --> 00:15:23,470
Gimme!

209
00:15:24,530 --> 00:15:26,650
Let go already!

210
00:15:27,430 --> 00:15:28,210
Hey, guys!

211
00:15:28,370 --> 00:15:29,310
Get over here!

212
00:15:29,550 --> 00:15:30,950
Do we look like we can?

213
00:15:36,090 --> 00:15:36,610
Huh?

214
00:15:36,610 --> 00:15:42,890
What was that?

215
00:15:42,890 --> 00:15:44,430
And why did they go chasing it?

216
00:15:45,350 --> 00:15:45,910
Whoa!

217
00:15:46,510 --> 00:15:48,790
So, it was a mage after all.

218
00:15:48,950 --> 00:15:50,370
Nope, there was no mage.

219
00:15:50,930 --> 00:15:53,610
This so-called living armor isn't controlled by magic,

220
00:15:53,970 --> 00:15:55,430
but by the creatures inside.

221
00:15:56,010 --> 00:15:56,510
Huh?

222
00:15:56,890 --> 00:15:57,910
Check this out.

223
00:15:58,330 --> 00:15:59,650
The armor has two layers,

224
00:15:59,830 --> 00:16:01,310
and look what's sandwiched between them.

225
00:16:03,170 --> 00:16:04,890
That makes the armor move.

226
00:16:04,890 --> 00:16:08,890
In the armor,

227
00:16:09,130 --> 00:16:10,270
these things link together.

228
00:16:10,730 --> 00:16:13,410
They form groups that act just like the muscles do in our bodies.

229
00:16:15,270 --> 00:16:16,770
On their own, they're weak.

230
00:16:17,050 --> 00:16:19,150
But together, they use the armor like a structure,

231
00:16:19,330 --> 00:16:19,790
and that

232
00:16:19,790 --> 00:16:22,050
is how they can move like us.

233
00:16:23,510 --> 00:16:24,890
They were aggressive with us

234
00:16:24,890 --> 00:16:27,250
because we happened to show up after they laid their eggs.

235
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:28,510
Seriously?

236
00:16:29,010 --> 00:16:30,970
Those icky things hatch from eggs?

237
00:16:32,110 --> 00:16:33,250
Born from eggs!

238
00:16:33,250 --> 00:16:34,090
Isn't that amazing?

239
00:16:34,530 --> 00:16:36,570
And I'm the one who found out about their secrets?

240
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:37,390
Until now,

241
00:16:37,490 --> 00:16:39,630
everyone thought living armor was controlled by magic.

242
00:16:39,910 --> 00:16:41,510
Wait till we tell the world about them.

243
00:16:41,670 --> 00:16:42,810
We're gonna blow some mines!

244
00:16:43,870 --> 00:16:44,890
You see that?

245
00:16:45,250 --> 00:16:46,750
How when he talks about monsters,

246
00:16:46,870 --> 00:16:48,030
he gets crazy eyes?

247
00:16:48,390 --> 00:16:49,370
Creeps me out.

248
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:51,290
Hey, don't be rude.

249
00:16:52,090 --> 00:16:52,570
Senshi,

250
00:16:52,810 --> 00:16:54,030
we can't eat the armor,

251
00:16:54,210 --> 00:16:55,650
but I bet we can eat these guys.

252
00:16:55,650 --> 00:16:58,090
They look pretty dang nutritious, don't they?

253
00:16:58,270 --> 00:16:58,690
Huh?

254
00:17:01,570 --> 00:17:04,930
There's no way anyone's eating that mysterious gooey gunk!

255
00:17:05,390 --> 00:17:06,210
Oh, Marcel.

256
00:17:06,670 --> 00:17:09,230
The first bite of a new food is always mysterious.

257
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:10,590
Where's your sense of adventure?

258
00:17:12,770 --> 00:17:14,490
That's a stupid adventure!

259
00:17:14,910 --> 00:17:15,810
I'll fix him up.

260
00:17:17,150 --> 00:17:18,510
Never cooked him before,

261
00:17:18,670 --> 00:17:20,390
so can't promise it'll be any good.

262
00:17:20,790 --> 00:17:22,110
Aw, thank you, Senshi.

263
00:17:22,770 --> 00:17:23,890
Hell no!

264
00:17:24,410 --> 00:17:26,470
What if those things are loaded with poison?

265
00:17:27,110 --> 00:17:29,530
I'm pretty sure any creature that poisonous

266
00:17:29,530 --> 00:17:31,710
wouldn't bother with hiding in a suit of armor.

267
00:17:32,670 --> 00:17:35,090
What the heck kind of meal do I make out of him?

268
00:17:36,010 --> 00:17:36,950
See that part?

269
00:17:37,190 --> 00:17:39,050
When I tried to pry it open with my hand,

270
00:17:39,130 --> 00:17:39,770
it wouldn't open.

271
00:17:40,430 --> 00:17:42,650
I ended up making a cut right along there.

272
00:17:42,890 --> 00:17:44,090
It couldn't close after that.

273
00:17:44,750 --> 00:17:47,210
You know how a mollusk has that adductor muscle thing

274
00:17:47,210 --> 00:17:48,030
to close their shells?

275
00:17:48,350 --> 00:17:49,230
That's what that is.

276
00:17:49,630 --> 00:17:51,330
So these are like shellfish.

277
00:17:52,110 --> 00:17:53,750
I got an idea.

278
00:17:54,170 --> 00:17:56,270
We'll need to pry him out of the armor first.

279
00:18:03,910 --> 00:18:04,710
Oh, no.

280
00:18:05,390 --> 00:18:05,950
They drowned.

281
00:18:06,570 --> 00:18:08,790
Guess we can't clean off the sand that way.

282
00:18:09,610 --> 00:18:11,070
And they didn't come from the sea,

283
00:18:11,270 --> 00:18:12,570
so maybe we don't need to.

284
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:15,610
Not sure if its organs are safe to eat,

285
00:18:15,710 --> 00:18:17,010
so they're going in the trash.

286
00:18:17,010 --> 00:18:20,730
I'll slice these ones up and make soup.

287
00:18:21,150 --> 00:18:22,350
Then heat some oil,

288
00:18:23,090 --> 00:18:26,270
add critter, season in the medicinal herbs for a stir-fry.

289
00:18:26,270 --> 00:18:34,070
The helmet critter is steamed.

290
00:18:34,070 --> 00:18:38,110
And these, classic style all the way.

291
00:18:45,330 --> 00:18:46,130
It's ready!

292
00:18:46,130 --> 00:18:56,390
What are you going to try first?

293
00:18:56,730 --> 00:18:59,950
Uh, uh, soup, I guess.

294
00:19:00,350 --> 00:19:02,850
Wait, does anyone have an antidote for food poisoning?

295
00:19:03,510 --> 00:19:05,190
Well, it doesn't smell bad.

296
00:19:05,930 --> 00:19:08,090
Pretty sure what I'm smelling is iron.

297
00:19:08,970 --> 00:19:09,470
Lyos.

298
00:19:09,470 --> 00:19:19,310
Why is everyone looking at me like that?

299
00:19:19,830 --> 00:19:21,570
You wanted to eat living armor,

300
00:19:21,770 --> 00:19:22,670
so there it is.

301
00:19:22,770 --> 00:19:23,150
Eat up.

302
00:19:23,290 --> 00:19:24,310
You discovered him.

303
00:19:24,450 --> 00:19:25,690
You get the first bite.

304
00:19:26,110 --> 00:19:26,910
Such an honor.

305
00:19:27,710 --> 00:19:29,410
You leave his corpse if he dies, okay?

306
00:19:29,790 --> 00:19:30,090
Okay.

307
00:19:30,090 --> 00:19:37,030
Did he die?

308
00:19:37,530 --> 00:19:38,410
It's delicious!

309
00:19:39,490 --> 00:19:40,930
Oh, my God, the flavor!

310
00:19:41,210 --> 00:19:42,290
It's so good!

311
00:19:42,550 --> 00:19:44,590
It didn't taste like anything at first but then!

312
00:19:44,730 --> 00:19:45,610
Oh, man!

313
00:19:46,270 --> 00:19:49,030
How long does food poisoning take to make you sick?

314
00:19:49,490 --> 00:19:50,550
Depends on the food.

315
00:19:50,550 --> 00:19:50,950
Ah!

316
00:19:55,590 --> 00:19:56,650
Not bad.

317
00:19:57,310 --> 00:19:59,290
Could use a condiment or three, maybe.

318
00:19:59,290 --> 00:20:00,930
How'd those come out?

319
00:20:01,530 --> 00:20:01,690
Huh?

320
00:20:02,290 --> 00:20:03,530
Uh...

321
00:20:03,530 --> 00:20:07,370
Well, at least these were stir-fried with medicinal herbs.

322
00:20:08,630 --> 00:20:08,770
Oh!

323
00:20:09,530 --> 00:20:09,710
Mm.

324
00:20:10,550 --> 00:20:11,150
Mm-hmm.

325
00:20:12,070 --> 00:20:13,010
Uh, and?

326
00:20:13,770 --> 00:20:15,370
It doesn't taste bad.

327
00:20:16,250 --> 00:20:17,410
Uh...

328
00:20:17,410 --> 00:20:18,290
Oh...

329
00:20:20,290 --> 00:20:22,290
Uh...

330
00:20:22,290 --> 00:20:23,290
Uh...

331
00:20:23,290 --> 00:20:27,290
Oh...

332
00:20:27,290 --> 00:20:29,570
How is it, Marsil?

333
00:20:29,970 --> 00:20:30,530
They...

334
00:20:30,530 --> 00:20:32,950
kind of taste like mushrooms.

335
00:20:33,330 --> 00:20:34,050
I know, right?

336
00:20:35,390 --> 00:20:37,390
I'm trying the steamed ones next.

337
00:20:37,870 --> 00:20:40,470
I bet these'll taste better than the grilled ones.

338
00:20:40,530 --> 00:20:41,210
Wow.

339
00:20:43,410 --> 00:20:44,570
Tastes like mold.

340
00:20:45,210 --> 00:20:47,530
Guess the helmet stink got cooked into them.

341
00:20:47,530 --> 00:20:47,970
What?

342
00:20:50,970 --> 00:20:51,410
Here.

343
00:20:51,910 --> 00:20:52,170
Hmm.

344
00:20:53,270 --> 00:20:56,070
In all my years of eating monster in this here dungeon,

345
00:20:56,410 --> 00:20:59,150
I never would have dreamed I'd eat critters like those.

346
00:20:59,570 --> 00:21:02,930
I doubt anyone dreamed living armor was really a type of shellfish.

347
00:21:03,370 --> 00:21:05,270
A weird type born from an egg case.

348
00:21:05,950 --> 00:21:08,570
Wouldn't it be neat to see what they're like right when they hatch?

349
00:21:09,230 --> 00:21:11,430
I bet they're so small you can barely see them.

350
00:21:11,430 --> 00:21:15,590
As they mature, they form their outer shells and find others like them.

351
00:21:15,950 --> 00:21:19,330
They figure out how to move, start exploring, make colonies.

352
00:21:20,390 --> 00:21:23,570
Maybe they line up like we saw them right before they mate.

353
00:21:24,310 --> 00:21:26,210
Something tells me they're hermaphrodites,

354
00:21:26,290 --> 00:21:28,930
and the biggest, healthiest colony lays all the eggs.

355
00:21:29,790 --> 00:21:31,450
Wait, I just thought of something.

356
00:21:32,110 --> 00:21:33,990
Whenever I saw suits of armor holding hands,

357
00:21:34,170 --> 00:21:35,490
I thought it was a dungeon prank,

358
00:21:35,570 --> 00:21:36,970
but maybe that was a mating ritual.

359
00:21:37,610 --> 00:21:38,650
Someone needs a nap.

360
00:21:38,650 --> 00:21:42,650
I was scared of living armor for so long.

361
00:21:43,130 --> 00:21:46,430
Turns out, it was just a fragile, delicious monster.

362
00:21:47,390 --> 00:21:49,710
Hey, I'm sorry your old sword got broken.

363
00:21:50,290 --> 00:21:51,650
That one's pretty neat, though.

364
00:21:51,930 --> 00:21:52,290
Hmm.

365
00:21:55,890 --> 00:21:56,890
Hey, Lyos.

366
00:21:57,610 --> 00:21:58,910
If you're taking that,

367
00:21:59,010 --> 00:22:00,850
want me to check it to make sure it's not cursed?

368
00:22:01,310 --> 00:22:02,590
No! Don't trouble yourself!

369
00:22:02,930 --> 00:22:04,390
It's not cursed at all, really!

370
00:22:04,650 --> 00:22:05,610
Totally not cursed!

371
00:22:05,830 --> 00:22:06,970
Like you can tell.

372
00:22:06,970 --> 00:22:10,270
Don't blame me if it turns out you get cursed.

373
00:22:13,370 --> 00:22:14,630
Wait up! I'm coming!

374
00:22:16,130 --> 00:22:18,270
So, with a new sword in hand,

375
00:22:18,510 --> 00:22:19,870
the journey continues.

376
00:22:21,830 --> 00:22:23,790
And as they descend into the dungeon,

377
00:22:24,150 --> 00:22:25,950
the other three have no idea

378
00:22:25,950 --> 00:22:28,390
their party has gained a new member.

379
00:22:28,390 --> 00:22:31,050
It's arock of death.

380
00:22:39,790 --> 00:22:41,390
And is that a new demon?

381
00:22:43,410 --> 00:22:45,610
Oh, H information.

382
00:22:45,690 --> 00:22:47,690
This is a new demon quiER pharmacy.

383
00:22:47,870 --> 00:22:49,530
What are you kidding me?

